WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:16.720
When my first guest had
her first breakthrough at age ten

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:19.440
she already knew
she'd be a superstar.

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:23.800
Now she's 19, and all has gone
to plan. Welcome, Zara Larsson.

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:28.800
Thank you so much.

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:35.840
Can you remember, before you were
famous, the first song you learned?

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:42.080
I'm sure it was a Carola song,
I think, actually...

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:45.720
-Or maybe Whitney Houston.
-Can you sing like Carola?

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:49.160
If I can do impression of Carola?

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:57.800
Oh, it was that good? Thank you!

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:07.160
-It's fantastic.
-Thank you so much.

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:10.320
Carola is awesome,
Whitney Houston is awesome.

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:17.480
Your rise to fame has been meteoric,
seeing as you're only 19.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:20.640
-But you've been around a long time.
-I have.

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:27.320
You're seen on one of the biggest
shows on TV in the US right now.

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:31.000
You got to open the Euro 2016.

00:01:31.160 --> 00:01:36.720
Now you're releasing a new album.
Do you still control your own time?

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:39.680
Is it easy to lose control
of your time?

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:45.160
It's a bit like that, but that's
because I have a tight schedule.

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:49.440
I have very little downtime,
which is a good thing.

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:53.520
I'm very busy, I do a lot of things,
a lot of fun stuff.

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:59.840
I love what I do, but I'm the type
of person who is totally unaware.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:07.080
Yesterday I was saying to my mom:
"I've got something tomorrow, right?"

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:09.960
And well, here I am, today.

00:02:10.120 --> 00:02:15.800
But I really don't know what
I've got scheduled, and I love it.

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:18.800
-So you want it that way?
-Yes.

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:22.680
-How far ahead do you think?
-Two days, tops.

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:25.440
You make a lot of money.
Do you manage it?

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:28.160
No.

00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:32.880
OK... Who is in charge of it?

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:36.080
-Mommy and Daddy.
-That's good.

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:40.320
They keep an eye on it,
and they wouldn't steal from me.

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:44.800
I'll probably be back here in
20 years and go, "Well, darn it..."

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:47.600
No, they would never do that.

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:50.320
Do you get like a fixed allowance?

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:55.400
Well, last night I called my mom
to ask for 200 kronor for the movies.

00:02:56.360 --> 00:03:02.080
But I mean, I still live at home,
I don't pay any bills.

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:05.200
I don't have a car,
not even have my license.

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:09.720
I have no expenses.
I only spend money on fun stuff.

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:15.920
If I had access to all the money,
there would be a lot of fun stuff.

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:19.400
I'd be like...

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:26.360
Have you bought anything expensive
that you've felt good about?

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:30.480
Well, yesterday, actually,
or the day before that...

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:34.920
I bought an apartment
for my grandmother.

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:39.240
-That's great.
-Well, you know, stuff like that.

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:41.840
That, to me, feels worth it.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:47.960
So do you call your mom and say,
"I need money for an apartment?"

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:52.880
No, it's all my mom. She asked me
if I thought we should do it.

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:57.560
And I said yes, of course Grandma
should have a little place.

00:03:57.720 --> 00:04:03.360
-Has Grandma moved in yet?
-No, it's a new build. Next year.

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:09.280
She'll be close to my cousins,
my sister...

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:13.600
Right now she's all alone
in my father's hometown.

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:16.080
I think this will be great for her.

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:18.800
-Was she happy to get it?
-Very.

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:22.160
-I bet.
-I bet she was, too.

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:28.960
I just hope she stays alive
long enough to move in.

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:34.800
It would be a real shame otherwise.

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:40.960
You are 19, so you could have
your driver's license.

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:43.360
-But you don't?
-No.

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:49.760
-Would you be a good driver?
-I know what you're getting at.

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:54.400
I'm getting at the fact that
you have some experience driving.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:59.520
Some, yes.
I've got a license to drive a moped.

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:03.320
Explain this to me,
because I'm not from Sweden.

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:06.920
-Only in Sweden do they have this...
-Really?

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:09.680
-You don't have mopeds in Norway?
-Yes...

00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:13.040
Yes, we do.

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:20.080
Yes, people do have mopeds.

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:22.960
If you're too scared
to ride a motorcycle.

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:27.880
But not this weird quadricycle,
which looks like a car...

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:32.080
It does look like a car,
but the max speed is 30 mph.

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:37.560
So I can go all over Stockholm,
as long as it's not a highway.

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:42.080
And how's that working out for you?

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:45.960
So well that the manufacturer
withdrew their endorsement.

00:05:51.560 --> 00:05:56.680
I've been in a few accidents,
let's put it that way.

00:05:56.840 --> 00:06:00.600
You're more like a serial offender.

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:04.520
That's how you see it?
I suppose, yes.

00:06:04.680 --> 00:06:09.000
Those of you who are from
Stockholm know the Klara tunnel.

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:13.840
-From City to the south...
-Lots of heavy traffic.

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:17.280
And as with most roads,
traffic flows both ways.

00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:23.280
But one tunnel goes one way only,
the other tunnel goes the other only.

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:26.000
So when you enter the tunnel,
that's it.

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:30.360
And I of course managed
to enter the wrong tunnel.

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:35.280
And this was... Let me explain!

00:06:35.440 --> 00:06:39.960
This was late on a Tuesday night,
there were no cars around.

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:42.760
And I had had my license for one day.

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:46.040
I was so happy,
driving my little car.

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:51.600
I was heading home,
but was unsure where I was going.

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:55.440
So I was like,
"Right or left? Right or left?"

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:59.440
And there's a huge sign
that says, "Right".

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:03.320
But I was like, "You know what?
Left feels right to me."

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:07.480
-Well, you must listen to your gut.
-So I enter the tunnel.

00:07:07.640 --> 00:07:11.440
I'm driving in the right lane,
because I know my stuff.

00:07:11.600 --> 00:07:15.160
Then an oncoming car
has to swerve and honks at me.

00:07:15.320 --> 00:07:19.520
And I'm like, "What the hell
are you doing in my lane?"

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:22.960
Then another car comes,
and we crash into each other.

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:27.040
That's when I realize
I'm in the wrong tunnel.

00:07:28.040 --> 00:07:32.080
But everyone was fine.
It could have been so much worse.

00:07:32.240 --> 00:07:35.560
I think the backseat is a great idea.

00:07:40.880 --> 00:07:44.840
-I'm sure your parents agree.
-Yeah...

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:50.800
I know you come from a home
where debate is encouraged.

00:07:50.960 --> 00:07:56.520
You've debated a lot, especially
with your dad, who's in the military.

00:07:56.680 --> 00:08:00.080
I read somewhere
you and your dad debate for hours.

00:08:00.240 --> 00:08:02.720
-Definitely.
-What do you discuss?

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:07.040
I mean, in my family, you know...
I talk a lot - I really do.

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:14.800
But I've got absolutely nothing
on my father. He has no off switch.

00:08:14.960 --> 00:08:17.440
We have a lot of discussions.

00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:23.320
But I can ask my dad a simple
question and get a whole lecture.

00:08:23.480 --> 00:08:25.600
He is very knowledgeable.

00:08:25.760 --> 00:08:29.480
Is he what feminists
like to call a "mansplainer"?

00:08:29.640 --> 00:08:34.720
Tell me about it! So many times
I've had to say, "Stop mansplaining!"

00:08:34.880 --> 00:08:41.240
A simple question can lead
to a 15-minute monologue.

00:08:41.400 --> 00:08:45.240
But he's amazing
and incredibly knowledgeable.

00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:49.960
He's probably the reason
I'm so interested in social issues.

00:08:50.120 --> 00:08:54.280
I want to learn about
our political environment.

00:08:54.440 --> 00:09:00.680
We talk a lot about, well,
feminism is a huge issue for me.

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:09.280
So that's great,
to have been brought up like that.

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:14.200
You've been very outspoken
about your feminist views.

00:09:14.360 --> 00:09:20.080
And you have a very political voice,
in addition to your singing voice.

00:09:20.240 --> 00:09:25.000
-And especially on social media.
-Yes.

00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:32.600
You tweet roughly, if not more,
then at least on a par with Trump.

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:38.920
-Yeah... I'm up there.
-It does get to be a lot.

00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:45.200
Do you ever feel...regret?

00:09:45.360 --> 00:09:48.440
-Do I what?
-Do you regret any of your tweets?

00:09:48.600 --> 00:09:52.280
Like, "I was too harsh there."

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:58.000
There was this one thing
that I had to delete.

00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:04.480
And it was after I saw the first
"50 Shades of Grey" movie.

00:10:04.640 --> 00:10:10.680
In my personal opinion - it's not my
type of movie - I thought it sucked.

00:10:10.840 --> 00:10:16.720
So I tweeted, "If you like this,
go here" - and linked to Pornhub.

00:10:18.840 --> 00:10:21.520
-Which is...
-But that's the only thing!

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:27.520
Which is one of many pornographic
sites online. There are more.

00:10:29.920 --> 00:10:32.200
Just to explain what it is.

00:10:32.360 --> 00:10:36.160
-I should explain it?
-No! I've explained it. No more!

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:40.520
-Please, no more about that!
-OK. I personally didn't regret it.

00:10:40.680 --> 00:10:46.080
But the label was like, "You're great
on Twitter, say whatever you want."

00:10:46.240 --> 00:10:50.240
"But stuff like that,
maybe it's unnecessary?"

00:10:52.120 --> 00:10:58.640
But when you say things like,
"I hate men" - you get into fights.

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:02.160
-I get into fights.
-Lots of grumpy men out there.

00:11:02.320 --> 00:11:06.520
And you hear from some them.
But you don't mean them personally?

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:12.600
Or maybe sometimes you do,
but do you mean all men or...?

00:11:12.760 --> 00:11:17.320
-Are you offended now?
-No, I'm unoffendable.

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:23.440
Just kidding! Of course I don't mean
all men, but this debate is boring.

00:11:23.600 --> 00:11:28.360
I just mean that macho culture
and men in general, in groups...

00:11:28.520 --> 00:11:31.760
...are scary, unpleasant,
and just annoying.

00:11:31.920 --> 00:11:35.000
Exactly.
And what happens when you...

00:11:37.720 --> 00:11:42.840
When you voice an opinion like that,
you get attacked by "trolls" online.

00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:45.480
-Absolutely.
-You get a lot of hate.

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:50.000
-Do you read it?
-To a certain extent.

00:11:50.160 --> 00:11:56.120
I think the more I am online,
just like all kids today...

00:11:56.280 --> 00:12:00.480
...the more I learn to kind of...

00:12:00.640 --> 00:12:05.480
On Twitter, there are
a lot of "eggs" for profile pictures.

00:12:05.640 --> 00:12:08.400
Right, the ones that are...

00:12:08.560 --> 00:12:13.360
Eggs are usually private profiles
with zero followers.

00:12:13.520 --> 00:12:17.360
-They're anonymous?
-Exactly, very anonymous.

00:12:17.520 --> 00:12:22.440
The ones who hide behind that
are those who write the worst stuff.

00:12:22.600 --> 00:12:28.240
It's easier to not be affected
by them, because it feels...

00:12:28.400 --> 00:12:30.760
You know? It doesn't feel real.

00:12:30.920 --> 00:12:37.960
I'd have tweeted just as much or even
more, if I didn't have my followers.

00:12:38.120 --> 00:12:45.520
Like I said, I grew up in a very
debate-friendly environment.

00:12:45.680 --> 00:12:49.280
That's just what I'm like.
I want to voice my opinion.

00:12:49.440 --> 00:12:54.080
I want to be heard and seen,
I want people to listen to me!

00:12:54.240 --> 00:13:00.800
So when you debate
and you go, for example...

00:13:00.960 --> 00:13:04.760
"I hate all men."
Does your dad agree?

00:13:04.920 --> 00:13:10.640
He understands exactly what I mean.
To get back to this irrelevant topic.

00:13:10.800 --> 00:13:15.760
When I say "all men," my dad isn't
offended, nor are my guy friends.

00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:19.760
I have men in my life
that I love and admire.

00:13:19.920 --> 00:13:25.760
But it's constantly this...
"Hey, not all men!" Yeah, we know!

00:13:25.920 --> 00:13:30.920
But if you're not a rapist,
or a wife beater, or a bully...

00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:35.480
If that's not you, then don't
get offended by it. That's all.

00:13:35.640 --> 00:13:37.920
You know what I mean?

00:13:40.280 --> 00:13:43.440
We need to understand
what privileges we have.

00:13:43.600 --> 00:13:46.440
I truly believe
that there are privileges.

00:13:46.600 --> 00:13:52.120
You're very privileged if you happen
to be white, male, rich, cis.

00:13:52.280 --> 00:13:56.240
So you need to check yours.
What are my privileges?

00:13:56.400 --> 00:14:01.600
I'm cis-gendered, with a body
that conforms to ideals...

00:14:01.760 --> 00:14:05.800
I'm straight, I'm white...
I need to be able to see that.

00:14:05.960 --> 00:14:09.040
-Thank you so much for being here.
-Thank you!

